A||||12||1FieroGTRacingInc||Carbed intake??||||5||
Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-05-2000||01:23 PM||||I'm having sooo much trouble still with my 87GT (LOST MOTOR topic) My ??'s are is there a 2.8 stock intake for a carb. from another car that i could pick up for my 2.8 that would work so i can eliminate my fuel problem's....  ????  thank's   steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-05-2000||01:41 PM||||No.  I would venture to say that you will have more troubles trying to kludge a carburetor setup onto your Fiero.  I <B>know</B> you're frustrated, but the FI system is <B>so</B> much better than carbs.<BR>Especially since the car was designed for FI.<P>To answer your original question, the closest thing I can think of is a sidedraft Carter YH, from a Corvair Spyder.  Lots of luck finding one of those, oops - BTW, it has 3 mounting studs (instead of 2 bolts like your throttle body).  Also, have fun making the carb work with 50psi gas from the fuel pump.  You need to do a lot of thinking before you do anything. ||||reg||4
Z||000002||cowans||09-05-2000||02:49 PM||||Finding a Carter side-draft might be easier looking at the marine applications. I have a Ford Interceptor V8 with 2 Carter side-drafts in my 16'Mahogany antique. Carb kits can be had at Daytona Parts Co. in Florida. Carbs are decent for the boat but I would stick to FI for auto/horsepower.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fsrowsell||09-05-2000||03:07 PM||||I have a Carb V8 and it works just fine... Fuel regulator controls the pressure<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||09-05-2000||03:41 PM||||Just my opinion, but I think trying to put a carb system on a 2.8 would be opening a bigger can of worms than what you have already.<P>Just recently, I replaced a badly hacked harness in my 84 SE.  The car started right up and ran fine after I hooked everything up.  Threw the air cleaner back on, and wouldn't you know it, it didn't want to start.  When I had a friend crank the motor, I could see the spark jump from the coil pack to the ground.  I cleaned the connection and it started back up fine.  Try to crank it in the dark and see if your spark is jumping somewhere and clean the coil connections.  Hope this helps.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-06-2000||01:35 AM||||Did any other car come with a 2.8 w/ a carbed setup??  camero??  s-10??||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||09-06-2000||12:51 PM||||1980 V6 X-cars (Citation, Phoenix, Omega, Skylark) have 60-degree 2.8's and no computer, if you really want to go low-tech.<P>Plan on doing away with the upper plenum and intermediate intake manifolds, and changing the lower intake manifold.  As someone mentioned earlier, don't forget to regulate the fuel pressure down to about 15psi. <P>(I can't believe I'm helping you with this, but you asked  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )     ||||reg||9
Z||000007||StuGood||09-06-2000||12:57 PM||||Wait a minute.  How will the distributor know what to do without inputs from TPS, MAP, etc.?  Okay, so now we'll be sure and get the big HEI distributor off an X-car to go with. <P>Tell you what, send me your upper plenum, intermediate manifold, lower manifold, fuel injectors, and OE distributor, and I'll send you all of the above parts.  I have them.<P>[Stu thinks - I'm <B>such</B> a generous guy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ! ]||||reg||3
Z||000008||Carrolles||09-06-2000||04:56 PM||||My 86 Pontiac 6000 had a 2.8 with a two barrel carb.||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-07-2000||12:12 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    I just kept messing and changing the plug's... wires... and a few new part's and...<P><BR>Finally..  It started all of a sudden... and it is running fine... BUT,  When I am justdriving at a steady speed (55mph) it start's to jump.. if that is the right discription...  maybe..  Jerky...???<P>Does anyone know what is causing that jerking at a steady speed??  <P>           thank's Steve...||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||09-07-2000||12:29 PM||||Edelbrock sells a 2 and 4 valve carburated intake for the 2.8 that accepts a Holley 4 barrel carb.<BR>I guess maybe the 4 valve version is for the TDOHC 3.4?||||reg||1
